        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "0d36b320-b179-5d22-8665-19a1bd95df19",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Gevherhan Sultan, Selim II, Suleiman the Magnificent, Hürrem Sultan, Murad III, Mehmed III\n- Roles: Ottoman sultans, family relationships\n\nFacts:\n- Suleiman the Magnificent, also known as Suleiman I and Kanunî Sultan Süleyman, was born on 6 November 1494 and died on 6 September 1566.\n- Suleiman the Magnificent was the tenth and longest-reigning sultan of the Ottoman Empire, ruling from 1520 until his death in 1566.\n- Gevherhan Sultan was the granddaughter of Suleiman the Magnificent and Hürrem Sultan.\n- Gevherhan Sultan was the sister of Sultan Murad III, who reigned from 1574 to 1595.\n- Gevherhan Sultan was the aunt of Sultan Mehmed III, who reigned from 1595 to 1603.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
